+/* Frame pipelining (LD_PIPELINE, default on; LD_PIPELINE=0 = the old
+ * synchronous present). The present used to submit the frame and then wait
+ * for the GPU to finish it (~4 ms a frame in a match) before the next frame
+ * could be recorded. With two frame contexts -- command allocator, transient
+ * rings and shader-visible descriptor heaps each -- the present only submits;
+ * the next frame records into the other context while the GPU draws this one,
+ * and the wait moves to the reuse of a context one frame later. Resources
+ * retired during a frame are released once that frame's fence has passed.
+ * Every other flush (ring overflow, readback, guest reference, movie) still
+ * waits for the whole queue, exactly as before. g.* always holds the current
+ * context's objects, so the draw code is unchanged. */
